{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>תחת</b> — Some say: from תנחת עלי ידך in Targum, [meaning] 'and he went down,' like נזיד, from ויזד [as] from the root נטע, and this is far-fetched."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The argument appears to involve proposed etymological connections between תחת, Targumic תנחת, נזיד, and ויזד, but the chain of reasoning is compressed and the final clause 'מן נטע' (from planted) is unclear in context; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:20.671809437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}